# Every secret the API reads, and the Key Vault secret it comes from.
#
# One source of truth, read by two things: `secrets.sh`, which puts values into
# the vault, and the deploy workflow, which wires them onto the Container App as
# Key Vault references. Adding a secret means adding a line here and nothing
# else.
#
#   ENV_VAR                     kv-secret-name              required|optional
#
# `required` fails the deploy if the vault does not hold it — the app cannot
# boot without it, so failing in CI is better than a crash-loop.
#
# `optional` is skipped when absent, and skipped means *unset*, not empty. That
# distinction is the whole reason this file exists: `defineTool` registration is
# gated on `envSet(...)`, so an absent key leaves its tool cleanly unregistered
# and the button simply is not there. An empty string registers the tool and
# then fails at call time, which reads to a user as "the product is broken"
# rather than "this is not configured".
#
# Key Vault secret names allow alphanumerics and dashes only, which is why they
# are kebab-case rather than matching the env var.
#
# NOT in this file, deliberately:
#   - NEXT_PUBLIC_* — inlined into the browser bundle at build time. Public by
#     definition; vaulting them would be theatre.
#   - AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT, WEB_APP_URL, *_MODEL, *_INTERVAL_MS, *_REGION,
#     NODE_ENV, PORT — configuration, not credentials. GitHub *variables*.

# ── Cannot boot without these ────────────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE_URL                   database-url                 required
CLERK_SECRET_KEY               clerk-secret-key             required
CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY          clerk-publishable-key        required
# Networkless JWT verification. Read by the Clerk SDK directly, not by any code
# in this repo — grepping for it finds nothing, which is not a sign it is unused.
# Without it Clerk verifies over the network on every request: correct, but a
# round trip per call.
CLERK_JWT_KEY                  clerk-jwt-key                optional

# ── Language models. Either one is enough; the second is a live fallback. ─
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY              anthropic-api-key            optional
OPENAI_API_KEY                 openai-api-key               optional
# An alternative to the Anthropic key, for routing through a gateway that does
# its own auth. `languageModelAvailable()` accepts either.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN           anthropic-auth-token         optional
# Only if the fallback should use a *different* account from OPENAI_API_KEY —
# separating the fallback's spend from the embeddings spend, say. Unset, the
# fallback reuses OPENAI_API_KEY.
OPENAI_FALLBACK_API_KEY        openai-fallback-api-key      optional
# Likewise for embeddings: unset, they reuse OPENAI_API_KEY. Worth its own key
# if embeddings run against a self-hosted or non-OpenAI endpoint.
EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY             embeddings-api-key           optional

# ── Signs the OAuth state parameter ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Every social connect flow is gated on this one value
# (`socialOAuthConnected = envSet('OAUTH_STATE_SECRET')` in index.ts), so
# without it no platform can be connected at all and the whole publishing path
# is unreachable. It is not a vendor key — generate one:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
OAUTH_STATE_SECRET             oauth-state-secret           optional

# ── Media generation. Each absent key removes its own tool. ──────────────
FAL_API_KEY                    fal-api-key                  optional
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY             elevenlabs-api-key           optional
HEYGEN_API_KEY                 heygen-api-key               optional
ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY             assemblyai-api-key           optional

# ── Publishing and attribution ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Without the aggregator key, publishing routes to a stub that returns a
# well-formed receipt and sends nothing. That is deliberate and useful in
# development, and actively misleading in front of a tester.
AYRSHARE_API_KEY               ayrshare-api-key             optional
DUB_API_KEY                    dub-api-key                  optional

# ── Native platform apps, for OAuth connect per platform ─────────────────
META_APP_ID                    meta-app-id                  optional
META_APP_SECRET                meta-app-secret              optional
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID             linkedin-client-id           optional
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET         linkedin-client-secret       optional
TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY              tiktok-client-key            optional
TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET           tiktok-client-secret         optional
X_API_KEY                      x-api-key                    optional
X_API_SECRET                   x-api-secret                 optional
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID              youtube-client-id            optional
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET          youtube-client-secret        optional

# ── The capture loop ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# All three, or none: the token sends, the phone number id addresses, and the
# app secret is what registers the inbound webhook. Without the last one a clip
# has no route back and the loop is one-directional.
WHATSAPP_TOKEN                 whatsapp-token               optional
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID       whatsapp-phone-number-id     optional
WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET            whatsapp-app-secret          optional
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN          whatsapp-verify-token        optional

# ── Trend sources. All absent means the deterministic stub, not live data. ─
YOUTUBE_API_KEY                youtube-api-key              optional
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID               reddit-client-id             optional
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET           reddit-client-secret         optional
PRODUCTHUNT_CLIENT_ID          producthunt-client-id        optional
PRODUCTHUNT_CLIENT_SECRET      producthunt-client-secret    optional
PINTEREST_ACCESS_TOKEN         pinterest-access-token       optional

# ── Everything else ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CANVA_CLIENT_ID                canva-client-id              optional
CANVA_CLIENT_SECRET            canva-client-secret          optional
GOOGLE_DRIVE_API_KEY           google-drive-api-key         optional
REDIS_URL                      redis-url                    optional
